FIXED (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08, generation v2-12900; commit 32ce58bd).  A pass before the capture promotion and the lowering, `Pl/Parser2.pm` `_rename_rereading_embedded_mys`, renames an expression-embedded `my` whose own statement mentions the name again (the OUTER variable -- a `my` is visible only after its statement) to `NAME__shadow__N` with exactly its binding's later uses (`_rename_decl_within`, the declaring statement skipped): the let then binds the fresh name and the statement's mentions keep reading the outer one.  New rename reason `:reread-shadow` (the seam shadow rename's counter, now reset before this pass; the eval capture alist strips `__shadow__N`).  "Mentions again" is the binder's count of the statement's mentions AS SPELLED NOW (`Pl::Binder::mentions_in`: element `$a[0]`, `$#a`, interpolation included -- the old text count missed the element spellings), ONE predicate (`_stmt_mentions_again`, now a method) for the pass and both arms; a `${x}` code brace in the scope keeps the old path.  Probed (scratch/s536e/pr/m6*.pl): the reproducer (`chomp(my @env = grep {...} @env)`, `foo(my $x = $x + 1)`), a loop, `push(my @a, $a[0] * 10, scalar(@a), $#a)`, a package global (`our @gl`), a hash, `my $l = (my $s = "[$s]")`, a string eval after it, closures per iteration -- tree = perl.  Guard while-my-closure-01.t row 10 (fails on the base).  Emission: perl-tests/magic.t + t/op/magic.t (magic.t:86), t/op/filetest.t (`open my $fh, ... or die "open $fh: $!"` -- the die's `$fh` is the global's, as in perl).
